5+ years of hands‑on experience with TypeScript or Python and strong OO/functional design skills. 4+ years of experience building and operating web service APIs (REST/SOAP/GraphQL) at scale. Demonstrated experience owning complex features or systems from design through production. Other Qualifications Comfort using AI‑assisted code generation tools (such as Cursor, Claude Code, GitHub Copilot) as part of the day‑to‑day development workflow. Deep understanding of distributed systems: concurrency, multithreading, consistency, fault tolerance, and performance tuning. Strong experience with API design and lifecycle: OpenAPI/Swagger, versioning strategies, backward compatibility, contract testing, and documentation. Experience with API gateway or edge patterns (routing, authentication/authorization, throttling, rate limiting, transformation, multi‑tenant concerns). Hands‑on experience with observability stacks (metrics, tracing, logging) and using them to improve latency and reliability. Familiarity with GraphQL and data‑oriented APIs; exposure to Data Cloud / analytical stores or MCP‑style agent integration patterns is a plus. Strong testing discipline (unit, integration, contract, performance) and experience with modern testing and observability stacks such as JUnit, ScalaTest, Postman, Mockito, Jacoco/Scoverage. Experience with cloud and containerized environments (e.g., AWS, Kubernetes) and CI/CD pipelines. Proven track record of mentoring engineers, leading technical discussions, and driving cross‑team initiatives. Ability to translate product and AI/agent requirements into robust API and backend designs. Comfort working in ambiguous problem spaces with a bias for pragmatic, iterative delivery. Workday Pay Transparency Statement (For EU Locations Only) Listed below is the base salary range applicable to this position. Workday pay ranges (and the precise pay offered to the successful candidate) are based on a number of objective criteria such as relevant experience and skills, and educa…",
