low automation, and localization—to improve both customer experiences and engineering productivity Experience Optimization: Partner with marketing, design, and product teams to deliver high-converting digital experiences that guide visitors toward meaningful actions such as Atlas adoption, sales engagement, and other conversion goals Platform Reliability & Performance: Own site performance, availability, observability, Core Web Vitals, CDN strategy, technical SEO, AI/search discoverability, and scalable architecture to ensure a world-class user experience Qualifications 10+ years leading large-scale web platform engineering, software development lifecycles, or enterprise website modernization initiatives Deep expertise with Adobe Experience Manager (AEM) Sites, including component architecture, content modeling, and enterprise-scale implementations Experience with the broader Adobe ecosystem (such as Adobe Target, RT-CDP, or AEM Assets) is strongly preferred Demonstrated success applying AI technologies, LLMs, or generative workflows to enterprise web platforms or engineering processes Proven people leader with experience managing distributed engineering organizations and blended internal/contractor teams Strong execution skills across roadmap planning, Agile delivery, release management, operational excellence, and continuous improvement Ability to translate business objectives into scalable technical solutions that drive measurable customer and revenue outcomes Deep understanding of modern web architecture, including headless/composable CMS patterns, APIs, web performance, accessibility, technical SEO, and emerging AI search optimization practices About MongoDB MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB's unified data platform, the most widely available, globally 