      url: "https://ie.linkedin.com/jobs/view/ai-software-engineer-future-talent-at-hrm-search-partners-4440963115",
      description: "We continue to see growing demand from clients for experienced AI Software Engineering Contractors to support enterprise-scale GenAI initiatives. If you anticipate completing your current assignment or expect to be available for a new project within the next three to six months, we would welcome a confidential conversation. In particular, we are keen to connect with contractors experienced in enterprise-grade Generative AI development. To discuss upcoming opportunities, please contact Shannon Begley at shannon.begley@hrmrecruit.com or apply below. Position: AI Software Engineer Type: Full-Time / Contract Department: Engineering / AI & Innovation Division Location: Dublin, Ireland (No visa sponsership) Key Responsibilities AI System Design & Optimisation: Design, implement, and optimise robust AI/GenAI systems including LLM-based applications, RAG pipelines, and complex agentic workflows. Microservices & API Development: Build and maintain high-throughput microservices and APIs using Python and standard orchestration frameworks such as FastAPI, LangChain, and LangGraph. Advanced Retrieval & Reasoning: Architect advanced, context-aware retrieval systems leveraging GraphRAG, knowledge graphs, semantic enrichment, and techniques optimized for complex, multi-hop reasoning. Agent Interoperability: Develop and integrate modern agent frameworks, implementing cutting-edge standards such as Model Context Protocol (MCP) and Agent-to-Agent (A2A) protocols for secure, tool-enabled automation. Infrastructure & Scaling: Build and maintain scalable infrastructure for training and deploying agentic models at scale utilising Google Cloud Platform (GCP), Vertex AI, and container orchestration platforms (Kubernetes/GKE). Model Evaluation & Guardrails: Apply advanced prompt engineering, continuous testing, and automated evaluation frameworks (e.g. LangSmith) to improve model performance, eliminate hallucinations, and ensure strict reliability. Responsible AI & Governance: Enforce complete compliance with ethical AI deployment practices, implementing system guardrails, privacy layers, and security measures to protect sensitive data. Collaboration & Leadership: Collaborate across engineering, data science, and product teams to deliver innovative solutions. Mentor junior engineers, champion clean coding standards, and contribute to reusable architectural patterns. About You: Education: Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, or a closely related quantitative field. 8+ years of professional software engineering experience At least 3 years of dedicated, hands-on experience building, deploying, and optimizing production-grade AI, Generative, and Agentic systems. Highly proficient in Python and industry-standard ML frameworks (e.g. PyTorch, TensorFlow). Deep expertise in LLM integration, advanced GenAI tooling, and semantic search. Practical experience with multi-agent ecosystems, semantic enrichment, and knowledge graphs. Cloud & Infrastructure: Proven cloud-native development background, with specific experience utilising GCP and Vertex AI. DevOps & CI/CD: Hands-on familiarity with Kubernetes (GKE), Terraform (Infrastructure as Code), and automated CI/CD pipelines (e.g. GitHub Actions, Harness). Architecture: Strong conceptual understanding of distributed microservice architectures, API gateway routing, and highly scalable system design. Soft Skills: Exceptional debugging, testing, and creative problem-solving skills, paired with a collaborative, proactive, and highly communicative approach.",
